From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vero Coder <vero@example.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pseudo: recover base path for O_PATH dirfds via /proc/self/fd

GNU tar >= 1.35 opens its working directory with O_PATH|O_DIRECTORY,
then calls openat(opath_fd, ".", O_RDONLY|...) to get a normal dir fd.
pseudo's normal openat path calls fxstatat() on the returned fd before
registering it; fxstatat fails on O_PATH fds so the fd is never stored
in fd_paths[], and the subsequent openat(opath_fd, ".") sees an unknown
base path, causing every *at() call inside do_package to fail with
"unknown base path for fd N".

Fix in base_path(): when fd_path(dirfd) returns NULL for a known-valid
fd, recover the real path with readlink("/proc/self/fd/<dirfd>") and
cache it via pseudo_client_path() for subsequent calls. readlink always
yields a canonical absolute path, so no trailing-slash / double-slash
artefacts are introduced into pseudo's path database.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vero Coder <vero@example.com>
---
 pseudo_client.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pseudo_client.c b/pseudo_client.c
--- a/pseudo_client.c
+++ b/pseudo_client.c
@@ -1524,6 +1524,23 @@
 			if (dirfd >= 0) {
 				basepath = fd_path(dirfd);
 			}
+			/* Fallback: O_PATH fds may not have been registered in fd_paths[]
+			 * (e.g. GNU tar >= 1.35 opens dirs with O_PATH|O_DIRECTORY, which
+			 * pseudo cannot fxstatat, so they never get stored).  Recover the
+			 * real path from /proc/self/fd and cache it for later calls.
+			 */
+			if (!basepath && dirfd >= 0) {
+				char proc_path[32];
+				static char resolved[PATH_MAX];
+				ssize_t rlen;
+				snprintf(proc_path, sizeof(proc_path), "/proc/self/fd/%d", dirfd);
+				rlen = readlink(proc_path, resolved, sizeof(resolved) - 1);
+				if (rlen > 0) {
+					resolved[rlen] = '\0';
+					basepath = resolved;
+					pseudo_client_path(dirfd, resolved);
+				}
+			}
 			if (basepath) {
 				baselen = strlen(basepath);
 			} else {
